It isn't, really. It's about on par with Snickersnee, and better than all
other general purpose artifacts except Grayswandir. Then there are Firebrand,
Frostbrand and Mjollnir, which are all better against monsters not resistant
to their effects, but far worse against the rest. And they destroy objects,
which you might or might not find relevant in the late game.

Since you're twoweaponing with the best type of general purpose onehanded
non-artifact weapon there is, your damage output is certainly high enough with
any of those artifacts, so the searching features would be reason enough to
stick with Excal, IMO.

